IMPORT prelude

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld): the provision index.
-- One entry for every part, division, schedule, section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph and defined term of the
-- deposited text (act-1954-003.txt), with its identifier as the text prints it when it is cited and its heading as the text prints it.
-- A subsection, paragraph or subparagraph is printed with no heading, so its heading is "".
-- A defined term has the term as its heading.
-- The entries were written by a script that reads the text file; the line numbers are the text file's own.

§ `The provision index`

DECLARE `Provision` HAS
    `identifier` IS A STRING
    `heading as printed` IS A STRING
    `kind of provision` IS A STRING
    `first line of the text file` IS A NUMBER
    `last line of the text file` IS A NUMBER

-- Provision OF identifier, heading, kind, first line, last line
`the provisions of the Act` MEANS LIST
    (`Provision` OF "part 1", "Preliminary", "part", 12, 12),
    (`Provision` OF "section 1", "Short title", "section", 13, 14),
